{"type":"assistant","uuid":"776e93c7-4f32-45b9-affb-adc51fe21929","session_id":"49832c05-f79c-4e04-a062-c17a28c93691","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"776e93c7-4f32-45b9-affb-adc51fe21929","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n## Summary\n\n### Bug Diagnosis\n\n**Location:** `TagsHelper.java`, method `removeTag()` (lines 88-94)\n\n**Root Cause:** The `removeTag()` method used `String.replaceAll()` with a plain string pattern:\n```java\ntitle = title.replaceAll(tagToRemove.getText(), \"\");\n```\nThis performs **substring** replacement. When removing `#test`, it also removes `#test` from within `#testa` and `#testb`, destroying those similar tags.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Buggy: `\"#test #testa #testb\"` → `\"a b\"` (destroys similar tags)\n- Fixed: `\"#test #testa #testb\"` → `\"#testa #testb\"` (only removes exact match)\n\n### Fix Applied\n\n**Two files modified:**\n\n1. **`TagsHelper.java`** — Added word boundary matching:\n   - Added `import java.util.regex.Pattern;`\n   - Changed `replaceAll(tagToRemove.getText(), \"\")` to `replaceAll(Pattern.quote(tagToRemove.getText()) + \"\\\\b\", \"\")`\n   - `Pattern.quote()` escapes any regex-special characters in the tag text\n   - `\\\\b` ensures only complete word boundaries match, preventing partial matches\n\n2. **`TagsHelperTest.java`** — Added test case `removesTagsFromNotePartialMatch()` that verifies removing `#test` doesn't affect `#testa` or `#testb`\n\n### Patch File\n\nThe complete patch is at:\n`/home/antu_shared/automated_program_repair_for_ui_bugs/runs/qwen_original_run3/bug-44/fix-tag-removal.patch`\n\n### Build Note\n\nThe project cannot be built in this environment due to network restrictions (jcenter.bintray.com, Maven Central, and Google Maven are unreachable). However, the Java syntax has been verified correct and the regex logic has been tested independently with a standalone Java program that confirms the fix works as expec